<section id="problems" class="py-20 sm:py-24 border-t border-line bg-page">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint mb-3">
        Sound familiar?
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] leading-[1.05] text-ink">
        Running more than one agent gets messy fast
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-card">
        <svg
          class="h-5 w-5 text-ink"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <line x1="6" x2="6" y1="3" y2="15"></line>
          <circle cx="18" cy="6" r="3"></circle>
          <circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3"></circle>
          <path d="M18 9a9 9 0 0 1-9 9"></path>
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          &ldquo;Two agents, one checkout, one broken build&rdquo;
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-[17px] font-medium tracking-[-0.015em] text-ink">
          One managed worktree per agent
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Agents edit separate trees, so one broken build never stops the other. Ferryx
          creates, names and removes each worktree under
          <code class="font-mono text-[13px]">.orca-worktrees/</code>, jailed to the repo root.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-card">
        <svg
          class="h-5 w-5 text-ink"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M6 8a6 6 0 0 1 12 0c0 7 3 9 3 9H3s3-2 3-9"></path>
          <path d="M10.3 21a1.94 1.94 0 0 0 3.4 0"></path>
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          &ldquo;Which tab is waiting for me?&rdquo;
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-[17px] font-medium tracking-[-0.015em] text-ink">
          Status on every pane
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          See which agent is working, waiting on you or idle without scanning tabs, and get a
          notification when one needs input. Detection covers 11 agents and also drives the
          macOS Dock attention badge.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-card">
        <svg
          class="h-5 w-5 text-ink"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8"></path>
          <path d="M3 3v5h5"></path>
          <path d="M12 7v5l4 2"></path>
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          &ldquo;I closed the window and lost a 40-minute run&rdquo;
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-[17px] font-medium tracking-[-0.015em] text-ink">
          Sessions that outlive the window
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Close the window, reload the UI, or let it crash &mdash; the headless Rust daemon
          keeps the agents running. On reconnect the output you missed replays from a 512 KiB
          ring buffer, and if it wrapped you are told there is a gap.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
